       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. A scheduled dose of 50 mg daily is five times the maximum labeled dose, and I can't find a clinical scenario where that would be appropriate. Overdoses at this level can cause profound hypotension and shock. They can also cause non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema, and the effects can last a long time because amlodipine's half-life is 30 to 50 hours. You also haven't given a clinical reason for it.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg once daily right now.\n- **Ask a pharmacist.** If you think this dose is warranted, a pharmacist or the attending should review it first. If they approve, it can be entered through their verification pathway.\n- **Treat a possible overdose.** If this is about an ingestion rather than a scheduled dose, it needs toxicology or poison control (1-800-222-1222 in the US) and not a routine order.\n\nTell me which of these you'd like, and I'll act on it."
      }
